70af9c21 sail-riscv 99e4993a -- vendored from TestRIG-private riscv-implementations/cheriot-sail (sail-riscv: CHERIoT DII step_exception drain loop fix), with local changes to sail-riscv/model/riscv_insts_cext.sail and riscv_sys_control.sail

Local changes since. The DPI build compiles generated_definitions/c/riscv_rvfi_model_RV32.c and never regenerates it, so every change must be in that file; source changes are mirrored in the .sail files so a regeneration keeps them:
- 2026-09-28 generated C only, try_execute: Error_not_rv32e_register handled as handle_illegal again, as the .sail source says (a hand-edit had made it RETIRE_SUCCESS).
- 2026-09-30 riscv_insts_hints.sail: C_ADDI_HINT, C_MV_HINT, C_ADD_HINT, C_SLLI_HINT raise Error_not_rv32e_register for x16-x31 (hint_rv32e_check); they never accessed their register, so a HINT naming x16-x31 retired as a no-op while the RTL traps (RV32E reserves those encodings). Found by TestRIG: c.addi x20, 0 = 0x0a01. Not yet reported upstream.
- 2026-10-04 src/cheri_sys_regs.sail + generated C (zext_is_CSR_defined): uccsr (0x8C0), sccsr (0x9C0) and mccsr (0xBC0) are not defined, so any access is an illegal instruction. They are legacy CHERI-RISC-V registers that CHERIoT drops; the CHERIoT RTL does not implement them and Microsoft's formal fork (ac58b3f8) disables the same clauses. Model finding, spec GAP-MF-1.
- 2026-10-09 CHERIoT-Ibex's implementation-defined CSRs (spec GAP-CS-3; the decision is that the model gains them): mconfigptr, mcounteren, menvcfg(h), mcountinhibit (all 13 bits, not just CY/IR), mhpmevent3-31, mhpmcounter3-31(h), hpmcounter3-31(h), tselect, tdata1-3, mcontext, mscontext, scontext, cpuctrlsts and secureseed, with Ibex's reset values and WARL masks (opentitan configuration), implemented as platform functions in new files sail-riscv/c_emulator/ibex_platform_csrs.{c,h} (included from riscv_platform.h; added to the Makefile's C_SRCS/C_INCS and to ../cheriot_sail/Makefile). Sources: riscv_sys_control.sail (`val ibex_csr_* = {c: ...}` externs; is_CSR_defined, check_Counteren, trap_handler (synchronous exception sets cpuctrlsts.sync_exc_seen/double_fault_seen), exception_handler CTL_MRET (clears sync_exc_seen), init_sys (reset)), riscv_insts_zicsr.sail (readCSR, writeCSR; a write to 0x320 also updates the model's own mcountinhibit), cheri_addr_checks.sail (ext_check_CSR: reads of hpmcounter3-31(h) need no ASR, as the CHERIoT ISA's CSR allowlist states). Generated C: the same calls as prologues of zis_CSR_defined, zcheck_Counteren, zext_check_CSR, zreadCSR, zwriteCSR, ztrap_handler, zexception_handler and zinit_sys. The counters' values, cpuctrlsts.ic_scr_key_valid and the mcounteren_writable_i pin are bench inputs (ibex_platform_set_*, pushed per step by the DPI bridge from the RVFI record). The .sail changes were type-checked by regenerating the C with Sail 0.19.1 (rems-project/sail 31cd0721) in a scratch copy; that regeneration is NOT a drop-in replacement for the vendored C, which was not generated from these sources (regenerating the unmodified tree gives about 240k diff lines: a different function set, e.g. the zget_config_print_* functions, and decoders of different size; earlier local changes exist only as hand edits), so the vendored C stays hand-patched.
